A class is a blueprint and an object is one thing built from it:

class Dog:
    def __init__(self, name):
        self.name = name
    def bark(self):
        return self.name + ' says woof'

rex = Dog('Rex') creates an object. __init__ runs automatically when an object is created, and self means the object itself. A class can inherit from another: class Puppy(Dog) gets everything Dog has.

A Future is a value that will be available later, such as data from a server. Mark a function async and use await to wait for a Future without freezing the screen:

Future<String> load() async {
  final text = await fetchText();
  return text;
}

await only works inside an async function. FutureBuilder is a widget that builds different UI for loading, error and done states of a Future.
